From 47ace586065bcc796560192db800d25a115a3836 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:55:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Mod menus: an empty or failed content load no longer locks
 the registries; the log and state say what a menu got

On a phone every mod menu (JSON or code) opened with no panel and no slot frames, and nothing said why. The menu
types, their screens and the other content registries are OnceLocks: content_root registered them even with no
mods and on its error path, with empty lists, so a first load that had no mods or failed locked them empty for the
whole process, and a later load with the mods could not fill them (the container then has no screen at all).
- content_root registers only a load that has mods and succeeded; a failed one leaves the registries alone.
- Loading content logs the mods, the error if any, and how many menu types, menu screens and code screens the
  registries hold; opening a mod menu logs its menu type, block, screen (json, code or none), whether the menu type
  and its screen are registered, whether the panel was found, the mod's GUI sprites in the atlas and the atlas size.
- horizon-ctl state has mod_menus with all of it (the last content load and the last mod menu opened), always.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RYe92n7spgy8vtm4CovRWA
